-- title:
--   Rank-cut certificate at D* — certified p-cells on [819/2048, 2355/4096]
-- statement:
--   Each conjunct is `CellOK p0 p1 l0 l1 l2 t0 t1` (bundle `RandomSizeStable_Stability_RankCutCert`) for one $p$-cell $[p_0, p_1]$ with explicit rational multiplier coefficients: for every $p \in [p_0,p_1] \cap (0,1)$, $\lambda(p) = (l_0 + l_1 p)/(1-p) + l_2 p/(\mu p - \Phi(p)) \ge 0$, every $\tau_j(p) = p(t_{0,j} + t_{1,j}p) \ge 0$, and for each of the nine families $j$ and all $0 \le a \le p \le A \le 1$ the two cut slacks $G_1, G_2$ are nonnegative. The cells of this statement are consecutive and cover $p \in [819/2048, 2355/4096]$. The coefficients come from a linear program; the claim is checked by evaluating first-order Taylor models in the kernel.
-- source:
--   Draw, Then Draw: The Metric Distortion of Random-Size Stable Lotteries, STOC 2027 submission 1342 (https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/1342.pdf), certified p-cells covering [819/2048, 2355/4096] (computation, not from the paper).

